claimed: script-cli -- the okay-script command line (operator ask
2026-09-07, designed in specs/okay-script.md).

run / render / build / check / serve / new. `build` is the half the
container never had: the same pages `serve` compiles per request,
rendered ONCE to plain files -- a static site with no JVM in the
deployment -- driven through Site itself so i18n, includes, meta and
static files come for free rather than being reimplemented.

Two things I expect to correct in the spec while writing:

- the binary. okay-deploy CANNOT depend on okay-script (the arrow
  points the other way), so `okay script ...` cannot live in
  okay-deploy's jar. okay-script's own assembly already carries
  okay-deploy, so THAT is the combined `okay` binary and okay-deploy's
  smaller one stays deploy-only.
- "build refuses a page that needs a request, naming the call". A
  session touch and a redirect are detectable precisely. `Web.current.
  form` is not -- Web is a data value with nowhere to put a refusal --
  so that limit gets said rather than claimed.

Files: okay-script Cli.scala + Build.scala + bin/okay, tests,
specs/okay-script.md, boards.
